<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan ups fuel oil bunker price by $4 per tonne.</title>
<headline>Taiwan ups fuel oil bunker price by $4 per tonne.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has raised prices of bunker fuel by $4 per tonne effective December 27, a company statement said on Friday.</p>
<p>Posted prices for 180-, 280- and 380-centistoke bunker fuel delivered at the ports of Keelung, Hualien, Taichung and Suao have been increased to $152. Term prices were also up by $4 to $149 per tonne.</p>
<p>Spot and term bunker C-grade was also raised $4, to $150 and $147 respectively.</p>
<p>CPC is Taiwan's sole supplier of bunker fuels.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703080).</p>
</text>
